00:00:00,010 --> 00:00:57,930
[ Watch on kissFlix.co ] 

1
00:00:58,115 --> 00:01:00,245
I don't want to be misunderstood anymore.

2
00:01:01,882 --> 00:01:03,238
We're almost there.

3
00:01:03,238 --> 00:01:07,202
I don't think she's noticed us yet.

4
00:01:10,441 --> 00:01:13,011
I'm going to be honest with Ms. Nam now.

5
00:01:17,168 --> 00:01:20,038
Pull yourself together, CEO Kang.

6
00:01:22,628 --> 00:01:24,558
The company is at stake.

7
00:01:52,558 --> 00:01:54,765
- Ms. Nam.
- What are you two doing here?

8
00:01:55,368 --> 00:01:57,438
We were just talking about work.

9
00:01:58,288 --> 00:02:01,406
You haven't left yet, Ms. Nam?

10
00:02:10,221 --> 00:02:11,987
I'm sorry to interrupt.

11
00:02:16,455 --> 00:02:17,855
Ms. Nam.

12
00:02:22,488 --> 00:02:23,888
Ms. Nam.

13
00:02:25,075 --> 00:02:26,767
Ms. Nam.

14
00:02:28,227 --> 00:02:29,894
Let's talk.

15
00:02:32,042 --> 00:02:33,708
It's not what you think.

16
00:02:33,708 --> 00:02:35,295
Then what is it?

17
00:02:37,977 --> 00:02:40,035
I'll explain everything once this is over.
So...

18
00:02:40,035 --> 00:02:41,745
"Later" again?

19
00:02:47,055 --> 00:02:49,355
I don't like being in a relationship like this.

20
00:02:50,562 --> 00:02:52,207
I can't...

21
00:02:55,421 --> 00:02:57,185
see you anymore.

22
00:03:02,688 --> 00:03:04,218
Ms. Nam.

23
00:03:23,815 --> 00:03:26,205
Isn't this what you wanted?

24
00:03:27,415 --> 00:03:28,815
You met her...

25
00:03:29,575 --> 00:03:32,542
to make things work with Ms. Nam, too.

26
00:03:32,542 --> 00:03:34,332
Not today.

27
00:03:37,101 --> 00:03:38,971
It wasn't like that.

28
00:03:40,115 --> 00:03:42,165
Da Reum is...

29
00:03:43,508 --> 00:03:46,518
a precious fan to me
before being someone I like.

30
00:03:47,555 --> 00:03:49,465
What have I done?

31
00:03:51,267 --> 00:03:53,383
It's hard to see her suffer more.

32
00:03:54,555 --> 00:03:56,405
Let's stop now.

33
00:04:02,975 --> 00:04:05,385
Actually, I couldn't do anything.

34
00:04:07,448 --> 00:04:09,518
Ha Gi didn't give me a chance.

35
00:04:23,201 --> 00:04:24,601
Kang Ha Gi.

36
00:04:33,159 --> 00:04:34,426
Ha Gi.

37
00:04:47,195 --> 00:04:52,238
I tried to use Jeong Yeon sunbae
to drive a wedge between you and Da Reum.

38
00:04:52,895 --> 00:04:54,295
I'm sorry.

39
00:04:55,077 --> 00:04:56,743
No.

40
00:04:58,695 --> 00:05:00,490
It has nothing to do with you.

41
00:05:02,455 --> 00:05:04,204
It's because of me.

42
00:05:06,934 --> 00:05:08,659
Kang Ha Gi.

43
00:06:38,105 --> 00:06:40,954
- Da Reum, let's go together.
- Okay.

44
00:06:42,831 --> 00:06:45,641
Da Reum, are you not feeling well?

45
00:06:47,104 --> 00:06:48,818
No, I'm fine.

46
00:06:50,251 --> 00:06:52,401
Da Reum, you're nervous, right?

47
00:06:54,165 --> 00:06:55,600
I'm nervous today too.

48
00:06:55,600 --> 00:06:59,765
But I have a good feeling about today.

49
00:06:59,765 --> 00:07:01,595
I have a hunch.

50
00:07:06,434 --> 00:07:08,778
Scarcity, scar...

51
00:07:08,778 --> 00:07:09,965
Why can't I pronounce it?

52
00:07:09,965 --> 00:07:13,972
- Scarcity, wanting what you can't have.
- Hello...

53
00:07:13,972 --> 00:07:17,324
- Team Leader Choi isn't answering either?
- I'm going to lose my mind.

54
00:07:17,324 --> 00:07:19,745
At this rate, I'll have to do
the whole presentation myself.

55
00:07:19,745 --> 00:07:23,685
Why are both the CEO and Team Leader Choi
out of reach?

56
00:07:23,685 --> 00:07:25,545
This is bad. What should we do?

57
00:07:25,545 --> 00:07:28,913
Don't panic.
Let's head out first, or we'll be late.

58
00:07:28,913 --> 00:07:31,614
Right. Let's go! We can't be late.

59
00:07:31,614 --> 00:07:34,297
Let's go. Everyone, get ready.

60
00:07:34,297 --> 00:07:35,907
Go on ahead.

61
00:07:35,907 --> 00:07:38,328
This is a real disaster.

62
00:07:43,105 --> 00:07:44,575
[HAN Customer Profiling Strategy PT]

63
00:07:47,514 --> 00:07:50,177
[HAN Customer Profiling Strategy PT]

64
00:07:54,441 --> 00:07:57,352
Hello. We...

65
00:08:07,445 --> 00:08:09,587
- Welcome.
- Hello.

66
00:08:09,587 --> 00:08:10,644
How have you been?

67
00:08:10,644 --> 00:08:13,812
Great. I've been very busy, thanks to you.

68
00:08:14,538 --> 00:08:16,109
I'll see you inside.

69
00:08:22,698 --> 00:08:28,435
We will now begin the PT
to select HAN's Korean partner.

70
00:08:30,845 --> 00:08:34,177
Today's presentations will be sent
to the Paris headquarters,

71
00:08:34,177 --> 00:08:38,298
and the board will make the final decision.

72
00:08:38,298 --> 00:08:44,033
Based on the draw, we'll start with SE:ON.

73
00:09:01,235 --> 00:09:05,659
The HAN customer, as defined by SE:ON, is...

74
00:09:05,659 --> 00:09:07,245
[Scarcity: Wanting what you can't have]

75
00:09:07,245 --> 00:09:09,772
Someone who responds to scarcity.

76
00:09:12,773 --> 00:09:14,365
[Scarcity: Wanting what you can't have]

77
00:09:14,365 --> 00:09:17,332
The moment it becomes a brand anyone can buy...

78
00:09:17,332 --> 00:09:19,305
Even the wording is the same.

79
00:09:19,305 --> 00:09:21,845
What's going on? Did our data leak?

80
00:09:21,845 --> 00:09:23,695
It must have been leaked.

81
00:09:24,406 --> 00:09:25,492
- This...
- We believe it...

82
00:09:25,492 --> 00:09:28,925
must be a brand that chooses its consumers.

83
00:09:28,925 --> 00:09:30,945
That's why SE:ON

84
00:09:30,945 --> 00:09:36,345
has already secured a showroom for HAN
on Korea's top luxury street,

85
00:09:36,345 --> 00:09:38,859
and by recruiting top stars as ambassadors,

86
00:09:38,859 --> 00:09:43,845
we have a perfect launch strategy in place.

87
00:09:48,601 --> 00:09:50,529
[APPELLO's HAN Strategy: Top Star Ambassadors]

88
00:10:00,341 --> 00:10:02,715
APPELLO, are you ready?

89
00:10:02,715 --> 00:10:05,565
- Yes, well...
- What do we do now?

90
00:10:05,565 --> 00:10:08,502
What are we going to do?
Do we just give the same presentation?

91
00:10:08,502 --> 00:10:11,249
It'll look like we're the ones who copied.

92
00:10:11,982 --> 00:10:13,196
Just a moment.

93
00:10:13,196 --> 00:10:16,561
If you don't present,
we'll assume you've withdrawn and move on.

94
00:10:16,561 --> 00:10:19,194
- No, we'll present.
- Wait a second.

95
00:10:19,194 --> 00:10:21,795
- We have to present.
- Hold on.

96
00:10:21,795 --> 00:10:23,665
- Let's talk for a second.
- Sit down first.

97
00:10:23,665 --> 00:10:25,236
Just a moment.

98
00:10:25,236 --> 00:10:26,735
Sit down for a second.

99
00:10:26,735 --> 00:10:28,504
- No, hurry up.
- What are we supposed to do?

100
00:10:28,504 --> 00:10:29,804
Let's go to the conference room.

101
00:10:29,804 --> 00:10:31,397
Just a moment.

102
00:10:31,397 --> 00:10:33,047
Sir.

103
00:10:35,791 --> 00:10:37,501
Play this one.

104
00:10:39,071 --> 00:10:41,007
What's this?

105
00:10:42,298 --> 00:10:43,828
The real proposal.

106
00:10:56,670 --> 00:10:58,352
I'm sorry I'm late.

107
00:10:58,352 --> 00:11:02,202
I'm Kang Ha Gi, CEO of APPELLO.

108
00:11:20,105 --> 00:11:21,788
[HAN Customer Profiling_Final]

109
00:11:28,681 --> 00:11:30,929
I'll begin the presentation.

110
00:11:30,929 --> 00:11:35,416
We believe HAN's customers
don't just consume trends.

111
00:11:35,416 --> 00:11:37,460
They set their own standards.

112
00:11:37,460 --> 00:11:39,415
They are...

113
00:11:41,011 --> 00:11:43,198
people with their own distinct tastes.

114
00:11:45,405 --> 00:11:47,391
When choosing clothes,

115
00:11:47,391 --> 00:11:50,389
they focus on
what completes their personal style.

116
00:11:54,523 --> 00:11:55,909
[Bukchon Hanok Showroom for HAN]

117
00:11:55,909 --> 00:11:58,661
<i>How did you narrow down these locations?</i>

118
00:11:59,583 --> 00:12:02,408
<i>I felt that CEO Han prefers places</i>

119
00:12:02,408 --> 00:12:06,995
<i>visited by people with clear tastes
rather than just what's trendy.</i>

120
00:12:08,865 --> 00:12:11,054
[Bukchon, Saint Germain, and HAN]

121
00:12:11,844 --> 00:12:14,634
<i>"People with clear tastes."</i>

122
00:12:21,196 --> 00:12:23,105
[TASTE: They don't consume trends]

123
00:12:23,105 --> 00:12:26,267
People who create and
steadily pursue their own style.

124
00:12:26,267 --> 00:12:31,292
APPELLO's profiling began right there.

125
00:12:31,292 --> 00:12:33,182
Such people recognize

126
00:12:33,182 --> 00:12:38,897
brands that have quietly built their identity
and taste over a long period of time.

127
00:12:42,844 --> 00:12:43,966
What the...

128
00:12:43,966 --> 00:12:47,873
In our analysis, HAN isn't a brand
people want because it's rare.

129
00:12:47,873 --> 00:12:51,737
It's a brand that recognizes their taste.

130
00:12:59,429 --> 00:13:00,655
[CONSUMER]

131
00:13:00,655 --> 00:13:02,009
[FAN]

132
00:13:13,213 --> 00:13:14,579
[FAN]
One day...

133
00:13:16,833 --> 00:13:19,198
an employee told me this.

134
00:13:21,513 --> 00:13:22,983
Fashion is...

135
00:13:25,813 --> 00:13:29,473
<i>I was just thinking
fashion brands are a lot like idols.</i>

136
00:13:29,473 --> 00:13:35,373
<i>They command the stage
and get hearts racing with their looks.</i>

137
00:13:35,373 --> 00:13:39,251
<i>Most of all, fans have loved them for years.</i>

138
00:13:39,251 --> 00:13:44,250
Fashion turns people into fans.

139
00:13:45,070 --> 00:13:46,523
That's what she said.

140
00:13:47,629 --> 00:13:53,583
When your heart starts racing,
you remember that object for a long time.

141
00:13:54,332 --> 00:13:57,383
So, we see HAN's customers not as consumers,

142
00:13:59,613 --> 00:14:01,277
but as lifelong fans.

143
00:14:03,072 --> 00:14:04,812
That is our conclusion.

144
00:14:12,033 --> 00:14:15,332
HAN is a brand that is ready
to meet those fans.

145
00:14:16,353 --> 00:14:18,228
APPELLO will work with you

146
00:14:19,115 --> 00:14:24,789
to create value
that those fans will remember forever.

147
00:14:51,106 --> 00:14:55,416
The two companies' perspectives were
distinctly different and very interesting.

148
00:14:56,013 --> 00:15:01,323
We'll decide on the Korean partner
after a board meeting in Paris.

149
00:15:26,486 --> 00:15:29,313
What a relief. Okay, everyone.

150
00:15:29,313 --> 00:15:32,003
Good job. We all did this together.

151
00:15:32,003 --> 00:15:34,497
Let's give ourselves a round of applause!

152
00:15:34,497 --> 00:15:36,653
We're not done yet.

153
00:15:36,653 --> 00:15:39,541
There's still a lot to do.
Let's go to the office.

154
00:15:50,248 --> 00:15:52,033
You bastard!

155
00:15:52,033 --> 00:15:55,393
Who the hell are you? Are you a double agent?

156
00:15:55,393 --> 00:15:57,753
Do you know how much money I spent on this?

157
00:15:57,753 --> 00:16:00,573
What are you going to do about this, bastard?

158
00:17:45,073 --> 00:17:47,463
What happened?

159
00:17:48,833 --> 00:17:51,063
I'm sorry I didn't tell you sooner.

160
00:17:54,373 --> 00:17:55,773
By any chance...

161
00:17:56,453 --> 00:17:58,523
was Team Leader Choi...

162
00:18:09,259 --> 00:18:11,089
Are you okay?

163
00:18:13,779 --> 00:18:15,469
For now...

164
00:18:21,919 --> 00:18:23,909
Let's talk later.

165
00:18:38,803 --> 00:18:40,353
Ms. Nam.

166
00:18:48,103 --> 00:18:49,995
I convinced Ha Gi to do it.

167
00:18:49,995 --> 00:18:55,603
We had to hide it from everyone at APPELLO,
including you, Ms. Nam.

168
00:18:55,603 --> 00:19:00,153
Insiders are the first to notice
when they're being suspected.

169
00:19:03,903 --> 00:19:05,171
I told you, didn't I?

170
00:19:05,171 --> 00:19:07,833
That I was betrayed by a best friend I trusted.

171
00:19:09,643 --> 00:19:11,803
It was SE.

172
00:19:11,803 --> 00:19:15,753
CEO Kang must be having a hard time
since he's in a similar situation.

173
00:19:16,629 --> 00:19:18,337
Team Leader Choi...

174
00:19:18,337 --> 00:19:23,706
I heard they're like family,
so I'm a bit worried.

175
00:19:23,706 --> 00:19:26,536
It feels like Ha Gi has lost everyone
around him.

176
00:19:36,013 --> 00:19:40,356
I'm asking because I don't know,
but has the CEO ever done this before?

177
00:19:40,356 --> 00:19:43,765
This is unprecedented in the history
of APPELLO.

178
00:19:43,765 --> 00:19:46,028
What's wrong, everyone?

179
00:19:46,028 --> 00:19:50,053
Da Reum,
CEO Kang didn't come to work today.

180
00:19:51,050 --> 00:19:53,523
What's going on? He didn't say a word.

181
00:19:53,523 --> 00:19:57,212
He never misses work, no matter what.
Even if he's dying...

182
00:20:02,564 --> 00:20:05,463
And Team Leader Choi is also absent
without notice.

183
00:20:05,463 --> 00:20:07,693
What on earth is going on?

184
00:20:22,732 --> 00:20:24,483
[CEO Kang Ha Gi, APPELLO]

185
00:20:30,023 --> 00:20:34,366
<i>The number you have dialed cannot be reached.
Please leave a message after the beep...</i>

186
00:21:12,413 --> 00:21:14,803
<i>- Don't run, don't run!
- Don't you love your uncle's house?</i>

187
00:21:14,803 --> 00:21:17,938
<i>- This isn't our house!
- It's okay. Yes.</i>

188
00:21:19,653 --> 00:21:20,689
<i>No!</i>

189
00:21:20,689 --> 00:21:22,869
<i>- Uncle.
- Uncle.</i>

190
00:21:25,109 --> 00:21:26,985
<i>Go ahead.</i>

191
00:22:25,193 --> 00:22:26,646
Ha Gi.

192
00:22:33,722 --> 00:22:37,452
I submitted my resignation,
so please process it.

193
00:22:42,383 --> 00:22:43,683
Tell me.

194
00:22:43,683 --> 00:22:45,583
Since when?

195
00:22:45,583 --> 00:22:48,953
No, why did you do it?

196
00:22:49,649 --> 00:22:51,532
Did SE offer to scout you?

197
00:22:51,532 --> 00:22:53,143
Why on earth did you do it?

198
00:22:53,143 --> 00:22:54,955
I had no choice!

199
00:22:56,963 --> 00:23:00,493
I'm a debtor who ruined my company,
and I had to feed my family...

200
00:23:01,643 --> 00:23:05,163
I'm sorry, but I needed the money.

201
00:23:05,163 --> 00:23:08,792
- I needed money to pay off my loans.
- I could have helped you!

202
00:23:09,442 --> 00:23:13,889
How much more pathetic do I have to get?

203
00:23:14,963 --> 00:23:18,952
Working under a rookie I hired,
and calling you "CEO"...

204
00:23:18,952 --> 00:23:21,056
Do you think that was easy for me?

205
00:23:21,056 --> 00:23:24,863
As you grew bigger,
I felt more and more insignificant.

206
00:23:24,863 --> 00:23:28,073
Do you know how miserable
I felt every single day by your side?

207
00:23:34,303 --> 00:23:35,882
Really?

208
00:23:39,093 --> 00:23:40,833
You and me...

209
00:23:44,622 --> 00:23:46,537
All the years we spent together...

210
00:23:50,123 --> 00:23:52,215
Did they mean that little to you?

211
00:23:56,363 --> 00:23:58,262
It was just your imagination.

212
00:23:58,923 --> 00:24:02,853
I regret not handing over the info.

213
00:24:03,463 --> 00:24:05,453
I should've just been a worse person.

214
00:25:11,053 --> 00:25:13,063
What's wrong?

215
00:25:15,693 --> 00:25:18,206
I couldn't even reach you.

216
00:25:53,646 --> 00:25:55,633
Pour it in the glass.

217
00:25:55,633 --> 00:25:57,659
I'm going to keep drinking.

218
00:26:06,393 --> 00:26:07,923
Seong Wook hyung...

219
00:26:09,553 --> 00:26:11,275
He said he needed money.

220
00:26:14,819 --> 00:26:17,269
He said it was hard being by my side.

221
00:26:20,573 --> 00:26:23,120
How could I not have known
things had gotten that bad?

222
00:26:25,199 --> 00:26:27,406
Even though I'm always right there...

223
00:26:30,499 --> 00:26:32,989
I never know when someone is falling apart.

224
00:26:39,906 --> 00:26:41,436
My mom was the same way.

225
00:26:45,003 --> 00:26:46,403
<i>I'm home...</i>

226
00:26:59,293 --> 00:27:00,693
<i>Mom.</i>

227
00:27:03,092 --> 00:27:04,492
<i>Mom.</i>

228
00:27:09,733 --> 00:27:15,483
My dad left home, and he never came back.

229
00:27:29,839 --> 00:27:34,279
I thought she'd get better with time.

230
00:27:44,153 --> 00:27:49,183
I thought she'd be okay because I was there.

231
00:27:50,933 --> 00:27:52,863
But she wasn't.

232
00:28:04,619 --> 00:28:06,075
<i>Mom!</i>

233
00:28:30,325 --> 00:28:31,888
<i>Mom!</i>

234
00:28:49,693 --> 00:28:51,943
I couldn't do anything.

235
00:28:56,013 --> 00:28:57,541
<i>Watch where you're going!</i>

236
00:28:57,541 --> 00:29:00,063
<i>Why did you cross without checking the light?</i>

237
00:29:05,993 --> 00:29:07,903
I'm always too late.

238
00:29:11,853 --> 00:29:14,083
In the end, I make everyone leave.

239
00:29:20,155 --> 00:29:22,673
Why is that your fault?

240
00:29:22,673 --> 00:29:24,703
They are in so much pain.

241
00:29:27,505 --> 00:29:29,335
I didn't even notice.

242
00:29:32,293 --> 00:29:35,363
I feel like I'm someone
who shouldn't be near anyone.

243
00:29:39,913 --> 00:29:42,152
Sir.

244
00:29:42,152 --> 00:29:45,302
At first, I thought you were very cold.

245
00:29:46,573 --> 00:29:48,543
But now I know.

246
00:29:49,593 --> 00:29:52,288
It's not that you're cold,

247
00:29:54,348 --> 00:29:57,038
it's that you're scared.

248
00:29:59,253 --> 00:30:01,083
Scared you'll lose someone again.

249
00:30:02,273 --> 00:30:04,063
Scared you'll be too late.

250
00:30:07,466 --> 00:30:10,055
If it's hard, you can say so.

251
00:30:10,055 --> 00:30:13,876
If you fall apart, just let it happen.

252
00:30:16,633 --> 00:30:19,283
I'll stay by your side till the end.

253
00:30:21,853 --> 00:30:24,297
If I'm important to you,

254
00:30:26,593 --> 00:30:28,543
protect me this time.

255
00:31:03,503 --> 00:31:05,664
[Kim Min Woo]
<i>Mi Mi, have you been very busy lately?</i>

256
00:31:05,664 --> 00:31:07,859
[Kim Min Woo]
<i>How about a drive this weekend? Go?</i>

257
00:31:07,859 --> 00:31:09,422
<i>Did I get rejected?</i>

258
00:31:09,422 --> 00:31:11,140
<i>Didn't we connect that day?</i>

259
00:31:11,140 --> 00:31:13,887
<i>♪ In the dream of my childhood ♪</i>

260
00:31:13,887 --> 00:31:16,111
<i>♪ Searching for the me I lost ♪</i>

261
00:31:16,111 --> 00:31:17,926
<i>♪ Leaving, away ♪</i>

262
00:31:17,926 --> 00:31:19,868
<i>♪ Beyond the blue sky ♪</i>

263
00:31:27,426 --> 00:31:29,523
Leaving him on read is one thing...

264
00:31:29,523 --> 00:31:31,483
But he's totally bounced
after you played hard to get.

265
00:31:31,483 --> 00:31:34,310
That's exactly how he ends up thinking
about me all day.

266
00:31:34,310 --> 00:31:36,775
He'll get even more hooked.

267
00:31:37,682 --> 00:31:40,163
Hooked? No way.

268
00:31:40,163 --> 00:31:41,863
You're the one who's hooked.

269
00:31:41,863 --> 00:31:45,697
I'm not into guys who give up this easily.

270
00:31:45,697 --> 00:31:49,893
If you're that worried, just text him first.

271
00:31:51,355 --> 00:31:53,063
Me?

272
00:31:53,063 --> 00:31:54,493
Why would I?

273
00:31:55,249 --> 00:31:59,622
This is why your love life is a mess.

274
00:32:09,683 --> 00:32:13,963
<i>Do you know why you're floundering
in her fishing pond?</i>

275
00:32:13,963 --> 00:32:15,915
<i>It's that impatience.</i>

276
00:32:15,915 --> 00:32:17,240
<i>It's because of your impatience.</i>

277
00:32:17,240 --> 00:32:19,042
Right, impatience.

278
00:32:19,042 --> 00:32:21,574
I'm too impatient.

279
00:32:21,574 --> 00:32:22,803
Impatience.

280
00:32:22,803 --> 00:32:28,007
<i>When you're about to give up,
she'll send a text to bait you again.</i>

281
00:32:31,183 --> 00:32:33,008
[Mi Mi]
<i>What are you doing?</i>

282
00:32:33,008 --> 00:32:34,143
I'm just...

283
00:32:34,143 --> 00:32:37,003
<i>Right then! Stop your fingers!</i>

284
00:32:37,003 --> 00:32:39,663
<i>- Don't check it or reply.</i>
- Why?

285
00:32:39,663 --> 00:32:42,693
<i>- Do the same to her.</i>
- The same?

286
00:32:48,989 --> 00:32:51,099
What should I do?

287
00:33:07,016 --> 00:33:09,766
My beloved APPELLO employees.

288
00:33:12,203 --> 00:33:15,112
A lot has been happening at our company lately.

289
00:33:15,112 --> 00:33:20,663
As you all probably know,
our company is currently...

290
00:33:20,663 --> 00:33:22,662
in a crisis. A crisis.

291
00:33:22,662 --> 00:33:23,843
What crisis?

292
00:33:23,843 --> 00:33:26,277
With the CEO and planning team leader gone,

293
00:33:26,277 --> 00:33:29,763
who can we trust and work for?

294
00:33:29,763 --> 00:33:34,567
At times like this, we must stick together.

295
00:33:34,567 --> 00:33:38,589
We have to protect this APPELLO we love,
don't we, everyone?

296
00:33:38,589 --> 00:33:40,964
So, who is it that we need?

297
00:33:42,180 --> 00:33:47,138
From now on, consult me for important matters.

298
00:33:47,138 --> 00:33:51,030
Just rely on me for everything important...

299
00:33:53,218 --> 00:33:54,803
You're here, sir.

300
00:33:54,803 --> 00:33:56,733
You're back, sir?

301
00:33:58,329 --> 00:34:00,661
I appreciate it, but I'm just coming to work.

302
00:34:00,661 --> 00:34:03,371
Why... You're here, sir.

303
00:34:06,322 --> 00:34:09,127
Let's get to work, everyone.

304
00:34:09,127 --> 00:34:10,753
Yes, sir!

305
00:34:13,489 --> 00:34:15,316
Welcome back.

306
00:34:34,006 --> 00:34:36,807
[HAN Korea Partner Final Selection Notice]

307
00:34:48,464 --> 00:34:51,838
[We are pleased to announce that APPELLO
has been selected as HAN's official partner]

308
00:34:53,076 --> 00:34:54,731
We did it.

309
00:34:54,731 --> 00:34:56,732
This is amazing!

310
00:34:56,732 --> 00:34:58,109
HAN's official partner!

311
00:34:58,109 --> 00:34:59,706
- Did you see the announcement?
- Yes!

312
00:34:59,706 --> 00:35:01,673
Did we really get it?

313
00:35:03,153 --> 00:35:05,580
Everyone, you all worked so hard.

314
00:35:05,580 --> 00:35:06,774
Congratulations.

315
00:35:06,774 --> 00:35:08,576
Did we really get it?

316
00:35:17,860 --> 00:35:21,256
[Fashion Hot Issue:
HAN Signs MOU with APPELLO as Korean Partner]

317
00:35:21,256 --> 00:35:24,319
[SE Trading Recovery of Tens of Billions
in Investment Remains Uncertain]

318
00:35:24,319 --> 00:35:26,073
[Users Flee SE:ON Platform After Launch,
Damaging Brand Trust]

319
00:35:26,073 --> 00:35:27,844
Kim Han Cheol!

320
00:35:28,783 --> 00:35:31,603
Do you have any idea
how much we've lost because of you?

321
00:35:31,603 --> 00:35:35,605
- I'm sorry, sir.
- Enough. Your contract is terminated.

322
00:35:36,462 --> 00:35:38,337
Sir!

323
00:35:52,403 --> 00:35:53,984
I look forward to working with you.

324
00:35:53,984 --> 00:35:56,573
Our Korean partner CEO.

325
00:35:58,343 --> 00:36:00,033
Thanks, sunbae.

326
00:36:00,033 --> 00:36:01,993
I solved the problem thanks to you.

327
00:36:03,263 --> 00:36:06,233
Kim Han Cheol is finished, right?

328
00:36:07,403 --> 00:36:10,713
Our collaboration wasn't so bad, was it?

329
00:36:13,683 --> 00:36:15,303
Are you heading back to France now?

330
00:36:15,303 --> 00:36:18,963
Yes. I'll start launch preparations
as soon as I'm back in Paris.

331
00:36:18,963 --> 00:36:22,483
I intend to do this right in the Korean market.

332
00:36:22,483 --> 00:36:24,723
I'll make sure everything is ready.

333
00:36:24,723 --> 00:36:27,919
Can you dispatch a representative
to our office?

334
00:36:27,919 --> 00:36:29,319
I'll do that.

335
00:36:36,463 --> 00:36:38,013
But...

336
00:36:38,783 --> 00:36:40,752
I still don't understand.

337
00:36:40,752 --> 00:36:44,033
Why did SE copy the fake version?

338
00:36:44,896 --> 00:36:48,853
You said you gave Team Leader Choi
the real proposal at the end.

339
00:36:52,083 --> 00:36:53,493
Well...

340
00:36:54,473 --> 00:36:56,626
I'm curious about that too.

341
00:37:05,301 --> 00:37:06,875
CEO Han!

342
00:37:16,480 --> 00:37:19,070
Do you have a moment?

343
00:37:21,424 --> 00:37:25,634
[Not HAN's Customers, but FANS:
Korean Spaces Where Tastes Linger]

344
00:37:31,553 --> 00:37:34,563
When did you prepare this?

345
00:37:35,573 --> 00:37:39,813
Working on the HAN project gave me some ideas,
so I organized them.

346
00:37:39,813 --> 00:37:43,583
This is more than just "organized."

347
00:37:46,233 --> 00:37:51,162
I'm a huge fan of the brand, and...

348
00:37:53,473 --> 00:37:58,691
I felt bad about being
so uncomfortable around you.

349
00:38:02,513 --> 00:38:04,353
Do you have plans today?

350
00:38:04,353 --> 00:38:06,712
Pardon? No.

351
00:38:06,712 --> 00:38:08,762
Then let's have dinner together.

352
00:38:11,053 --> 00:38:12,783
I have to return the favor.

353
00:38:14,053 --> 00:38:16,333
Ms. Nam, what do you like?

354
00:38:16,333 --> 00:38:20,223
I eat everything. What about you?

355
00:38:20,932 --> 00:38:22,933
Korean food.

356
00:38:22,933 --> 00:38:24,523
Korean food.

357
00:38:25,609 --> 00:38:30,071
Then do you want to go to a place I recommend?

358
00:38:38,793 --> 00:38:41,744
- It's hot.
- Thank you.

359
00:38:46,081 --> 00:38:50,033
These are all side dishes my mom sent me.

360
00:38:50,033 --> 00:38:52,652
My mom's cooking is amazing.

361
00:38:54,006 --> 00:38:55,610
I'll enjoy the meal.

362
00:38:55,610 --> 00:38:58,382
I've been craving a home-cooked meal...

363
00:38:59,606 --> 00:39:03,736
You don't have any family in Korea, right?

364
00:39:06,733 --> 00:39:08,973
When I was a senior in high school...

365
00:39:08,973 --> 00:39:12,239
my mom remarried, so I went to study abroad.

366
00:39:12,239 --> 00:39:14,609
I didn't want to live with my stepfather.

367
00:39:17,105 --> 00:39:18,996
We're not in touch.

368
00:39:21,346 --> 00:39:24,213
It must have been hard on your own.

369
00:39:24,213 --> 00:39:27,112
At least I didn't struggle with money.

370
00:39:27,112 --> 00:39:28,654
I'll enjoy the food.

371
00:39:28,654 --> 00:39:30,284
Enjoy your meal.

372
00:39:34,833 --> 00:39:38,143
- It's delicious.
- Right? Please, have more.

373
00:39:44,093 --> 00:39:45,493
It's good.

374
00:39:50,713 --> 00:39:56,253
At first, my only goal was
to be the "Best Employee,"

375
00:39:56,253 --> 00:39:59,864
but now that I'm working,
I'm looking for my own path.

376
00:39:59,864 --> 00:40:03,094
It'll become clearer over time.

377
00:40:04,453 --> 00:40:07,168
You said this last time.

378
00:40:07,168 --> 00:40:12,343
That failing your first brand helped you
realize what you're capable of.

379
00:40:13,253 --> 00:40:17,765
Those words really stuck with me.

380
00:40:17,765 --> 00:40:21,815
I want to try different things and even fail.

381
00:40:22,433 --> 00:40:23,833
That's good.

382
00:40:28,793 --> 00:40:33,723
I see why Ha Gi likes you, Ms. Nam.

383
00:40:35,959 --> 00:40:41,089
You're warm and comforting
like a home-cooked meal.

384
00:40:43,553 --> 00:40:45,023
Me?

385
00:40:46,093 --> 00:40:49,159
Ha Gi's a pretty cool guy for recognizing that.

386
00:40:51,153 --> 00:40:53,123
So much so that I want to steal him.

387
00:40:54,493 --> 00:40:55,893
Pardon?

388
00:40:57,173 --> 00:40:59,443
So, make sure things go well.

389
00:41:04,177 --> 00:41:05,693
You startled me.

390
00:41:49,962 --> 00:41:51,362
Mom.

391
00:41:53,100 --> 00:41:55,042
You used to like these beans.

392
00:41:58,193 --> 00:42:00,005
For my sake...

393
00:42:02,093 --> 00:42:04,443
at least have some before you go.

394
00:42:17,012 --> 00:42:19,542
This is the chicken you like.

395
00:42:20,413 --> 00:42:23,573
What's this? You didn't say anything.

396
00:42:23,573 --> 00:42:27,363
I was just passing by and thought of you.

397
00:42:28,966 --> 00:42:30,796
Let's go in. I'm hungry.

398
00:42:39,219 --> 00:42:41,142
My mom's memorial table...

399
00:42:42,845 --> 00:42:44,782
It's your first time seeing it, right?

400
00:42:49,173 --> 00:42:50,863
You jerk.

401
00:42:56,513 --> 00:42:59,396
You've been going through this alone
without even telling me?

402
00:43:53,263 --> 00:43:54,813
I didn't know...

403
00:43:56,883 --> 00:43:59,853
you went through so much after I left.

404
00:44:06,743 --> 00:44:08,873
I'm sorry for telling you so late.

405
00:44:11,443 --> 00:44:13,113
Me too...

406
00:44:15,223 --> 00:44:18,256
I guess I didn't have the courage
to face what happened back then.

407
00:44:20,709 --> 00:44:27,139
But thanks to Ms. Nam, I changed my mind.

408
00:44:28,343 --> 00:44:30,313
I don't want to lose anyone anymore.

409
00:44:32,223 --> 00:44:34,093
Everyone else left, but...

410
00:44:36,463 --> 00:44:38,353
I don't want to lose you and Ms. Nam.

411
00:44:39,903 --> 00:44:41,973
I really don't.

412
00:45:01,833 --> 00:45:03,993
I hate myself so much.

413
00:45:06,523 --> 00:45:08,393
I'm so much worse than you.

414
00:45:13,803 --> 00:45:18,433
You two are precious to me, too.

415
00:45:21,563 --> 00:45:23,311
So...

416
00:45:26,743 --> 00:45:28,993
make Da Reum happy.

417
00:45:56,663 --> 00:45:59,453
And you'd better invite me
to the next memorial service.

418
00:46:00,343 --> 00:46:01,647
I'm really hurt.

419
00:46:01,647 --> 00:46:03,333
I will.

420
00:46:14,292 --> 00:46:16,829
[The Target: The Last Aim Scenario]

421
00:46:18,103 --> 00:46:21,774
<i>Director Park Chan Dong's film contract.
Congratulations, Chan.</i>

422
00:46:49,943 --> 00:46:51,530
<i>Whatever you decide,</i>

423
00:46:51,530 --> 00:46:56,943
<i>I hope you choose
something you truly want to do.</i>

424
00:46:56,943 --> 00:46:59,313
<i>Just for yourself.</i>

425
00:47:10,423 --> 00:47:12,900
[Teo]
<i>Hyung, we've been practicing together.</i>

426
00:47:12,900 --> 00:47:15,973
[Teo]
<i>Come by if you're curious.</i>

427
00:47:31,909 --> 00:47:34,303
It's not over.

428
00:47:34,303 --> 00:47:35,703
For me, either.

429
00:47:55,080 --> 00:47:56,710
Chan hyung.

430
00:48:09,343 --> 00:48:10,805
Thank you.

431
00:48:10,805 --> 00:48:14,433
I didn't expect you to actually come.

432
00:48:17,782 --> 00:48:20,772
What are you here for? To cheer us on?

433
00:48:23,723 --> 00:48:25,873
There's still something I want to do.

434
00:48:30,463 --> 00:48:32,823
- Are we just here to fill your nostalgia?
- Hyung.

435
00:48:32,823 --> 00:48:36,193
The guy who ran away first after we
disbanded has no right to feel regret.

436
00:48:38,523 --> 00:48:40,693
We never waited for you.

437
00:48:50,636 --> 00:48:52,906
Then why did you leave my part empty?

438
00:48:58,209 --> 00:49:00,443
It's natural for you to hate me.

439
00:49:00,443 --> 00:49:04,293
But I won't run away anymore.

440
00:49:05,363 --> 00:49:07,566
I know I'm being thick-skinned, but...

441
00:49:08,643 --> 00:49:10,093
just once,

442
00:49:11,403 --> 00:49:13,193
just this once.

443
00:49:14,123 --> 00:49:16,373
Let's give it our all together.

444
00:49:22,705 --> 00:49:24,105
Together?

445
00:49:25,579 --> 00:49:28,349
Let's try again.

446
00:49:29,868 --> 00:49:31,359
Hyung!

447
00:49:49,225 --> 00:49:50,625
Hyung.

448
00:49:59,619 --> 00:50:01,429
Seriously...

449
00:50:20,299 --> 00:50:23,429
Why was I refunded? I still have time left.

450
00:50:24,799 --> 00:50:27,518
Because you make me uncomfortable,
Min Woo.

451
00:50:27,518 --> 00:50:30,598
- Why am I uncomfortable?
- Just because.

452
00:50:30,598 --> 00:50:32,528
I don't want to waste my emotions.

453
00:50:33,779 --> 00:50:35,692
Then let's stop.

454
00:50:37,032 --> 00:50:39,482
Let's stop playing hard to get.

455
00:50:40,299 --> 00:50:43,436
Am I not capable? Can't I kiss? I'm good at it!

456
00:50:43,436 --> 00:50:45,492
Oh my, what is he saying?

457
00:50:45,492 --> 00:50:49,062
From now on, I'll call when I want to
and come see you when I miss you.

458
00:50:51,505 --> 00:50:53,565
I give up.

459
00:50:53,565 --> 00:50:57,651
Since I've surrendered,
let's stop this tug-of-war.

460
00:50:57,651 --> 00:50:59,019
You should do the same, Mi Mi.

461
00:50:59,019 --> 00:51:00,419
Pardon?

462
00:51:01,072 --> 00:51:02,722
What did you say?

463
00:51:04,825 --> 00:51:06,535
I'm saying we should date.

464
00:51:33,979 --> 00:51:39,169
Oppa, don't you miss the other DNX members?

465
00:51:41,299 --> 00:51:43,491
Would they even want to see me?

466
00:51:47,459 --> 00:51:50,069
Well, I wouldn't know that.

467
00:52:24,636 --> 00:52:27,859
<i>How did you get in here?</i>

468
00:52:27,859 --> 00:52:30,084
<i>Delivery.</i>

469
00:52:30,084 --> 00:52:32,499
<i>Could you leave it over there?</i>

470
00:52:32,499 --> 00:52:34,219
<i>Sure.</i>

471
00:52:34,219 --> 00:52:37,349
<i>But what about Roy's part?</i>

472
00:52:38,959 --> 00:52:40,193
<i>Let's just leave it empty.</i>

473
00:52:40,193 --> 00:52:42,119
<i>He might come back.</i>

474
00:52:42,119 --> 00:52:45,076
<i>How? We don't even know if he's dead or alive.</i>

475
00:52:45,076 --> 00:52:46,773
<i>Don't say that.</i>

476
00:52:51,399 --> 00:52:53,409
<i>What if we find him?</i>

477
00:53:16,330 --> 00:53:21,809
Oppa, you think you shouldn't see them
even if you miss them, right?

478
00:53:22,945 --> 00:53:24,709
Because you feel sorry?

479
00:53:26,119 --> 00:53:28,193
I'm the one who ruined it.

480
00:53:28,193 --> 00:53:30,545
It'd be shameless of me to show up.

481
00:53:30,545 --> 00:53:33,171
Then just go with an apologetic face.

482
00:53:34,652 --> 00:53:36,764
Or go with an embarrassed face.

483
00:53:36,764 --> 00:53:38,139
Well...

484
00:53:38,139 --> 00:53:40,089
You could even go crying.

485
00:53:41,299 --> 00:53:43,999
Why are you deciding everything?

486
00:53:43,999 --> 00:53:49,769
You don't know if they'll curse,
get angry, or welcome you back.

487
00:53:53,785 --> 00:53:55,455
I'm just scared.

488
00:54:05,999 --> 00:54:09,769
Do you know why I went
as far as doing deliveries to find you, oppa?

489
00:54:11,865 --> 00:54:14,513
Because rather than being
disappointed after meeting you,

490
00:54:16,432 --> 00:54:19,855
regretting not seeing you
for the rest of my life

491
00:54:20,505 --> 00:54:22,954
was a hundred times scarier.

492
00:54:24,699 --> 00:54:27,481
The members might feel the same way.

493
00:54:27,481 --> 00:54:31,849
They might resent you,
but they still want to see you.

494
00:54:32,986 --> 00:54:35,096
If you're really sorry...

495
00:54:36,432 --> 00:54:39,285
don't just keep hiding.

496
00:54:39,285 --> 00:54:42,595
Give them a chance to resent you in person.

497
00:54:56,739 --> 00:54:59,820
I could be a great cook
if I had a cookbook like this.

498
00:54:59,820 --> 00:55:00,899
Should I buy it for you?

499
00:55:00,899 --> 00:55:03,269
No, it's okay. I don't need it.

500
00:55:12,299 --> 00:55:13,970
[VOIR]
It's CEO Han.

501
00:55:19,179 --> 00:55:21,748
She must have done an interview
while she was in Korea.

502
00:55:23,719 --> 00:55:24,925
Let's go.

503
00:55:24,925 --> 00:55:27,405
Wait. Let's watch a bit more.

504
00:55:34,753 --> 00:55:36,822
[HAN, and her questions]

505
00:55:39,522 --> 00:55:42,394
[When your environment changes,
you'll be asked different questions]

506
00:55:42,394 --> 00:55:45,275
[Those questions made me stronger
and helped me grow]

507
00:56:10,087 --> 00:56:11,900
Do you want to go to the beach
to see the sunrise?

508
00:56:11,900 --> 00:56:15,209
I'd love to. Where to?

509
00:56:15,209 --> 00:56:18,329
I guess we should go to the East Sea?

510
00:56:18,329 --> 00:56:20,809
So we'll stay together until dawn then?

511
00:56:22,869 --> 00:56:25,880
I guess so.

512
00:56:28,855 --> 00:56:30,525
An overnight trip?

513
00:56:38,502 --> 00:56:41,865
I just really want to see the sunrise.

514
00:56:46,409 --> 00:56:48,139
I'll think about it.

515
00:56:49,829 --> 00:56:51,229
Okay.

516
00:56:51,869 --> 00:56:54,887
Then, go on in.

517
00:57:06,576 --> 00:57:08,888
It's late. You should get going.

518
00:57:09,882 --> 00:57:11,508
Okay.

519
00:57:13,755 --> 00:57:14,968
I'm leaving.

520
00:57:14,968 --> 00:57:16,368
Yeah.

521
00:57:18,575 --> 00:57:20,560
- I should go.
- Yeah.

522
00:57:39,079 --> 00:57:40,919
Sir.

523
00:57:41,849 --> 00:57:42,869
Yes?

524
00:57:42,869 --> 00:57:47,393
I don't have a cat,

525
00:57:47,393 --> 00:57:50,022
but I have something interesting at my place.

526
00:57:51,049 --> 00:57:52,539
Do you want to come see it?

527
00:57:57,441 --> 00:57:59,070
Something interesting?

528
00:58:07,771 --> 00:58:09,171
What is it?

529
00:58:11,229 --> 00:58:12,719
She's making me nervous.

530
00:58:16,717 --> 00:58:18,309
Let's go.

531
00:58:39,569 --> 00:58:41,783
Don't be too surprised.

532
00:58:44,389 --> 00:58:46,022
- Why here?
- Pardon?

533
00:58:46,022 --> 00:58:48,759
You said there was underwear inside.

534
00:58:49,348 --> 00:58:51,098
But why?

535
00:59:05,995 --> 00:59:07,665
Ta-da!

536
00:59:15,709 --> 00:59:18,102
Wait...

537
00:59:18,102 --> 00:59:20,597
What on earth is all this?

538
00:59:21,689 --> 00:59:25,778
It's my 12-year history of fangirling.

539
00:59:36,749 --> 00:59:39,806
I didn't want to hide anymore.

540
00:59:40,536 --> 00:59:46,216
This is a part of me too,
and I'm also the Nam Da Reum who likes you.

541
00:59:47,021 --> 00:59:49,195
I wanted to show you that.

542
00:59:55,210 --> 00:59:56,735
That's a relief.

543
00:59:56,735 --> 00:59:58,995
Now I can sleep with a clear conscience.

544
01:00:01,397 --> 01:00:03,157
Honestly...

545
01:00:04,545 --> 01:00:05,949
What is it?

546
01:00:05,949 --> 01:00:11,179
Since you confessed first,
I'm telling you all my secrets too.

547
01:00:12,868 --> 01:00:15,138
Honestly, I'm a bit jealous.

548
01:00:19,181 --> 01:00:22,001
I'll cut back on it now.

549
01:00:33,969 --> 01:00:36,859
I know it was the driving force in your life.

550
01:00:39,095 --> 01:00:41,265
I should be thankful to Chan.

551
01:00:44,689 --> 01:00:48,399
He's the one who brought us together.

552
01:00:52,309 --> 01:00:56,421
Then from now on, my bias is...

553
01:00:57,355 --> 01:00:58,941
Kang Ha Gi?

554
01:01:58,600 --> 01:01:59,839
I'm heavy.

555
01:01:59,839 --> 01:02:01,529
You're not heavy at all.

556
01:03:45,759 --> 01:03:49,756
I tried olive lemon shots
and Greek yogurt for a while,

557
01:03:49,756 --> 01:03:51,855
but I gave up.

558
01:03:51,855 --> 01:03:53,090
Why?

559
01:03:53,090 --> 01:03:56,234
I had no energy
because I wasn't eating any carbs.

560
01:03:57,559 --> 01:03:59,474
Eat as much as you want.

561
01:03:59,474 --> 01:04:01,309
You felt too light.

562
01:04:07,879 --> 01:04:11,109
Stop staring. I'm getting embarrassed.

563
01:04:12,810 --> 01:04:14,318
What were you thinking?

564
01:04:14,318 --> 01:04:16,502
Seriously!

565
01:04:17,799 --> 01:04:20,907
It's not the first time we've slept together.
Why are you like this?

566
01:04:20,907 --> 01:04:24,650
What do you mean? When did we?

567
01:04:25,766 --> 01:04:29,236
In the CEO's office after the welcome dinner.

568
01:04:46,439 --> 01:04:50,278
I stayed up all night and fell asleep too.

569
01:04:50,278 --> 01:04:54,772
No wonder it felt familiar.

570
01:05:00,492 --> 01:05:05,126
I really didn't know back then
that things would turn out like this.

571
01:05:54,619 --> 01:05:56,129
Sir.

572
01:05:57,339 --> 01:05:58,739
Yeah?

573
01:06:01,171 --> 01:06:02,571
Well...

574
01:06:03,399 --> 01:06:07,298
What if I applied for the Paris assignment?

575
01:06:42,599 --> 01:06:45,347
<i>I know this is a great opportunity
for Ms. Nam...</i>

576
01:06:45,347 --> 01:06:46,807
<i>but I still don't want her to go.</i>

577
01:06:46,807 --> 01:06:49,300
<i>Trust me, I've done long distance.
You two will definitely break up.</i>

578
01:06:49,300 --> 01:06:50,463
<i>- Hey!
- You scared me!</i>

579
01:06:50,463 --> 01:06:53,539
<i>Don't they kiss each other
on the cheek over there?</i>

580
01:06:54,126 --> 01:06:57,725
<i>One, two, three, four, five. Let's go!</i>

581
01:06:57,725 --> 01:06:58,766
<i>Come back, Roy.</i>

582
01:06:58,766 --> 01:07:01,077
<i>Let's stop running away.</i>

583
01:07:01,077 --> 01:07:02,949
<i>I couldn't even root for you.</i>

584
01:07:02,949 --> 01:07:06,067
<i>I hated myself for resenting you.</i>

585
01:07:06,067 --> 01:07:07,598
<i>It felt like he was talking about me.</i>

586
01:07:07,598 --> 01:07:09,640
<i>It's supposed to be a message
from you to your fans,</i>

587
01:07:09,640 --> 01:07:12,347
<i>but it also feels like
what I've always wanted to tell you.</i>

588
01:07:12,347 --> 01:07:16,305
<i>If I go, you're not letting go, right?</i>

